+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Wda1aTg4aFbSfqJLnV56Sp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mg9RUbDXEk9xfo1nP9qrgH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/CONTRACT.md","content":"# CONTRACT: Constraint-Based Event Scheduler\n\nThe `schedule(events, rooms, options)` function and its behaviors. Each criterion has a verifying test.\n\n## Types & API\n- [ ] Exports `schedule` as a named export from `src/index.ts` → test: import works, is a function.\n- [ ] Also exposes `Scheduler` class and `createScheduler` factory (bonus surface) → test: both callable, produce same result.\n- [ ] Re-exports types `Event`, `Room`, `ScheduleOptions`, `Assignment`, `ScheduleResult` → test: compiles (build).\n\n## Core placement\n- [ ] Single event fits in a room within the window → test: 1 assignment, correct room/start/end, start==window.start, end==start+duration.\n- [ ] Event end must be <= endTime; an event whose duration exceeds the window is unscheduled → test: duration > window → unscheduled.\n- [ ] Event start must be >= startTime → test: assignment.startTime >= options.startTime always.\n- [ ] `attendees` defaults to 1 when omitted → test: event w/o attendees fits in capacity-1 room.\n\n## Capacity (Rule 1)\n- [ ] Event with attendees > every room capacity is unscheduled → test: unscheduled list contains it.\n- [ ] Event is only ever placed in a room whose capacity >= attendees → test: across all assignments, room.capacity >= event.attendees.\n\n## Time window (Rule 2)\n- [ ] Every assignment satisfies startTime >= options.startTime and endTime <= options.endTime → test: property check over a multi-event result.\n\n## Room gaps (Rule 3)\n- [ ] Two events in the same room are separated by at least `gap` minutes (end-to-start) → test: two events, gap respected.\n- [ ] Default gap is 15 when options.gap omitted → test: two back-to-back events in a single room have >=15 min gap.\n- [ ] gap of 0 allows back-to-back events → test: gap:0 places second event exactly at first's end.\n\n## Prerequisites (Rule 4)\n- [ ] If B requires A, A finishes (end + gap) before B starts → test: B.start >= A.end + gap.\n- [ ] Prereqs hold across different rooms too → test: A in room1, B in room2, ordering respected.\n- [ ] If a prerequisite is itself unscheduled, the dependent is unscheduled → test: A can't fit → B also unscheduled.\n- [ ] A prerequisite referencing a non-existent event id makes the dependent unscheduled → test: B requires \"ghost\" → B unscheduled, no throw.\n- [ ] Diamond prereqs (D needs B and C, both need A) respected → test: D.start >= max(B.end,C.end)+gap.\n\n## Preferred room (Rule 5)\n- [ ] preferredRoom honored when feasible → test: event placed in its preferred room though others are free.\n- [ ] preferredRoom is a hint: if it can't fit there, event still scheduled elsewhere → test: preferred room too small → placed in a larger room, still scheduled.\n\n## Cycles (Rule 6)\n- [ ] Direct self-reference (A requires A) throws → test: expect throw.\n- [ ] Two-node cycle (A->B->A) throws → test: expect throw.\n- [ ] Longer cycle (A->B->C->A) throws → test: expect throw.\n- [ ] Acyclic graph does NOT throw → test: no throw.\n\n## Batch optimization (Rule 7 / Behavior)\n- [ ] Maximizes number scheduled: a case where naive in-input-order greedy strands an event but a better room assignment fits all → test: all events scheduled.\n- [ ] Best-fit capacity: small events don't hog the only large room needed by a large event → test: both fit.\n- [ ] Events that genuinely cannot be placed go to `unscheduled` (no throw) → test: over-subscribed window → some unscheduled, function returns.\n- [ ] No event appears in both assignments and unscheduled; every input event appears in exactly one → test: partition property.\n- [ ] No two assignments overlap (with gap) in the same room → test: global non-overlap property over a packed scenario.\n\n## Robustness\n- [ ] Empty events → empty result → test: {assignments:[], unscheduled:[]}.\n- [ ] Empty rooms → all events unscheduled → test.\n- [ ] Determinism: same input → identical output across runs → test: two calls deep-equal.\n\n## Tooling\n- [ ] `npm run build` clean.\n- [ ] `npm run lint` clean.\n- [ ] `npm test` all pass.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":302,"cache_read_input_tokens":25865,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":302},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66a03b1b-28ed-4449-a853-a4ec1c26571b","uuid":"1cd4335c-64ad-4ce1-9a13-75bd175d1342","request_id":"req_011CbWXYypYijUQngzkgb1DC"}
